    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d170">

                <pb facs="0250" n="216" sameAs="frus:frus1870/pg216"/>

                <note rend="inline">CORRESPONDENCE BETWEEN THE DEPARTMENT OF STATE AND THE NORTH
                    GERMAN LEGATION AT WASHINGTON.</note>
                <note rend="inline" type="source">No. 170.</note>
                <head>Baron Gerolt to Mr. Fish.</head>
                <p>By order of the King, the North German government begs the United States
                    Government to allow that the United States legation at Paris may protect Germans
                    in France during the war.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">[The above was handed to me personally, by
                        Baron Gerolt, at my residence, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1870-07-18"
                            >Monday, July 18</date>, about 6½ p. m.</dateline>
                    <lb/>
                    <signed>H. F.]</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
